d3-force — vendored third-party dependency
==========================================

File:    d3-force.js
Package: d3-force@3.0.0  (https://github.com/d3/d3-force)
License: ISC (reproduced below)

Why it is checked in
--------------------
The console is served straight out of the daemon jar and must work with no network access and no
build step, so the dependency is committed rather than fetched or bundled at build time.

The file is the pre-bundled ES module, which already inlines d3-force's own dependencies
(d3-quadtree, d3-dispatch, d3-timer) and imports nothing at runtime. That matters: the plain
`+esm` builds served by some CDNs keep live CDN imports and would break offline.

Regenerating
------------
    curl -s "https://esm.sh/d3-force@3.0.0/es2022/d3-force.bundle.mjs" -o d3-force.js

After regenerating, verify it is still self-contained — this must print nothing:

    grep -o 'from *"[^"]*"' d3-force.js


